    <subfield code="a">USB key card in pocket, containing "Documentado/undocumented" (video performance by Guillermo Gómez-Peña and Gustavo Vazquez) and "Oaxacalifornia border treatments" (soundscape by Zachary James Watkins).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A USB drive included with the book contains Doc/Undoc's original sound art and video"--Page 4 of cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">DOC/UNDOC Documentado/Undocumented Ars Shamánica Performática features Guillermo Gómez-Peña's performance texts and Felicia Rice's relief prints and typography, accompanied by Jennifer González's critical commentary. The deluxe edition is housed in a hi-tech aluminum case containing a video by Gustavo Vazquez, an altar, and a cabinet of curiosities. Opening the case triggers light and Zachary Watkins' interactive sound art.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Introduction. Collaboration and metamorphosis : an invitation / Felicia Rice -- Colaboradores -- Critical commentary. DOC/UNDOC : transgress, transcend, transform / Jennifer A. González -- The artists' book -- Prints -- Performance scripts : catalog of the texts by Guillermo Gómez-Peña that are embedded in the prints -- Cabinet of curiosities : ars shamánica performática -- Video. Documentado/undocumented / Guillermo Gómez-Peña and Gustavo Vazquez -- Sound art. Oaxacalifornia border treatments : soundscape / Zachary James Watkins.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"MacArthur Genius Guillermo Gómez-Peña and award-winning book artist Felicia Rice create a multi-media border-crossing hybrid: the book as performance art"--</subfield>
    <subfield code="c">Provided by publisher.</subfield>
  </datafield>
